<h1>About this site</h1>

<p class="lede">
  Illustrative training material for Herkimer County. Nothing here is adopted county
  policy. This page explains how the site is put together and how to move around it.
</p>

<h2>What the site shows</h2>
<p>
  Four county jobs, each with one scenario in which an employee used an AI tool. Four
  policy flavors, each a fixed configuration across four operational dimensions:
  Security, Accountability, Efficiency, and Innovation. Every job is written against
  the same four flavors, so a scenario that is a violation under one flavor may be
  compliant under another. The flavor in force determines the outcome, not the
  scenario alone.
</p>

<h2>How to move around</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Overview</strong> lists the four jobs and the four flavors, with each
    job's verdict under each flavor.</li>
  <li><strong>Jobs</strong> takes you to one job. Its main page places the four
    flavors side by side; the row of flavor tabs opens any one of them on its own.</li>
  <li><strong>Policies</strong> starts from the matrix of flavors by dimension, and
    from there into a single flavor applied to all four jobs.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Comparing two flavors</h2>
<p>
  On a job's main page, all four flavors are readable as they stand. If your browser
  runs the site's scripts, a small pair of menus appears above the columns: choose two
  flavors and the view narrows to those two, marking the paragraphs whose wording
  differs. Everything remains readable without it — the comparison is a convenience,
  not a requirement.
</p>

<h2>Printing and PDFs</h2>
<p>
  Most pages carry a download link to a pre-rendered PDF: a single job under a single
  flavor, all four flavors for one job as a packet, or the full compendium. Pages also
  print directly from the browser.
</p>

<h2>Accessibility</h2>
<p>
  The site is plain HTML and works with keyboard navigation and screen readers. Colour
  marks each flavor but never carries meaning on its own; verdicts, labels, and
  dimension settings are always stated in words.
</p>
